  "remediation": [
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-SEC001",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The permission guard checks its mapping generation before mprotect. Both a stale-region unit test and a real fork inside a read callback passed on Linux."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-SEC002",
      "status": "fixed",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Linux closes from fd 3 after redirecting standard streams. The fallback blocks user signals and marks a private descriptor table close-on-exec. A Linux test exercised this fallback and checked that the parent retained its original descriptor flags. Native macOS acceptance is pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-SEC003",
      "status": "fixed",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Only a spawn-time Linux pidfd or a Windows handle can receive a termination request. The POSIX fallback never signals a numeric PID. Linux covered both identity classes. Native Darwin acceptance is pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-SEC004",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Both sides require whole-process isolation. The parent also verifies process scope for each required measure. A worker with an extra thread failed ordinary Worker::start even with an empty required list."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-SEC005",
      "status": "fixed",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "After lowering the primary token, the library checks effective tokens and rejects an incomplete inspection. Earlier thread handles are reused only if Windows confirms object identity. The impersonating-sibling regression was compiled. Native Windows execution is pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-API001",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "open_channels and startup inspect the calling thread’s table. An integration role opens eight files in its private table and checks that each appears."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-FUN001",
      "status": "fixed",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "A dedicated Unix waiter remains responsible for collection after startup failure or unsuccessful termination. A Linux worker held on a FIFO returned false and was collected after the parent closed the writer. Native macOS acceptance is pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-BLD001",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Affected parents wait for a positive PID, retry EINTR, require a matching wait result and distinguish normal child exit from a signal."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-BLD002",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Memory-lock refusal and refusal of a second namespace now produce distinct partial-check reasons. The outer assertion must still pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-BLD003",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The channel test uses exclusive creation. The isolation test claims its own mode-0700 directory and removes only its owned file and the empty directory."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-BLD004",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Linux tests expect Confirmed in the initial PID namespace and Unknown where an external tracer is invisible. Worker requirements respect the same distinction."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-DOC001",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The technical guide and public rustdoc distinguish protected native allocations, heap-backed WASM buffers, inherited references and guarded cleanup."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-API002",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Linux integer arguments use libc::c_ulong in variadic slots. The seccomp filter pointer retains its native type. Test probes follow the same ABI."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-SEC006",
      "status": "fixed",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Before pipe admission the launcher drops its original process handle and keeps only wait and termination rights. The Windows test reads GrantedAccess and compares the exact mask. Native execution is pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-BLD006",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "CI checks fuzz formatting and lints, and passes each lockfile to RustSec. The corresponding local checks passed. The changed workflow still needs to run on GitHub."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-014-BLD007",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The crate selects panic=abort, LTO and one code-generation unit for standalone releases. A consuming workspace selects its own profile. The linked release API harness passed."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-008-API001",
      "status": "fixed",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "Aliases, unknown bits and malformed platform-specific channel names are rejected before claiming the one-shot role. The canonical parser was fuzzed on Linux. The Windows-only cases need native execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-010-SEC001",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The transient guard and the owning allocation both check the fork generation. Ordinary owners, callback return and a foreign-generation permission operation were tested on Linux."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-010-BLD002",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The nested role communicates separate reasons for unavailable locking and namespace creation. Both are distinguishable from a successful subcase."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-010-BLD004",
      "status": "fixed",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The Unix assertions use protocol results, EOF, a parent-controlled FIFO and observed collection. Short wall-time thresholds and retries were removed. The Windows termination case needs native execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "AUD-010-DOC001",
      "status": "verified",
      "fixCommit": null,
      "verificationCommit": null,
      "evidence": "The WorkArea rustdoc and technical guide describe WASM heap allocation. The fallback also passed four checks in V8."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native Windows, macOS and Linux AArch64 have no test result for this working tree. Android and iOS have compile-time coverage only.",
    "On macOS and Linux without a spawn-time pidfd, an unresponsive worker can outlive end(false). A Unix waiter remains until exit. Leave POSIX wait-status ownership to the library.",
    "Windows token inspection describes the time of the check. A later impersonation can change a thread’s effective rights.",
    "Line coverage is measured on Linux x86-64. ASan excludes four locking-related checks. Miri ran one wipe test."
  ]
